<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tunisia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tunisian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tunisia is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, corresponding largely to the ancient region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, later the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a>, whose empire stretched from the Atlantic to Tunisia. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it was the scene of the final <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> defeat in North Africa, which accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> place in its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tunisia.jpg" alt="Tunisia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Various Wikimedia Commons' contributors · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tunisia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
